      "verdict_json": "{\"adjudicated_at\": 1791834177, \"applied_covenant_clauses\": [\"Evidence policy satisfied via authenticated, digest-matched authority snapshots from distinct registered USGS and EMSC hosts with required authority classes.\", \"Remedy policy satisfied because independently operated USGS and EMSC catalogs both identify the same seismic event at magnitude 8.0 or greater with materially compatible origin time and location.\", \"Requested consequence is proportionate because ENTER_READ_ONLY seeks intensity 60, below the cap of 80, and the claim specifies a 20-minute duration, below the two-hour maximum.\"], \"case_digest\": \"7c8b781d794c3696b92c92c10e3db33303570d4e9bea43b24e20f4c83b4caa9d\", \"covenant_digest\": \"7d6317c7325b38290a21fcb053d09c9ba31783168a672c7774a6d44622db3b8a\", \"decision\": \"BREACH_PROVEN\", \"findings\": [\"USGS snapshot usgs-kamchatka-2025-v1 is authentic, HTTP 200, digest-matched, and reports event us6000qw60 with magnitude 8.8, origin time 2025-07-29T23:24:52.483Z, latitude 52.4948, longitude 160.2395, and depth 35 km.\", \"EMSC snapshot emsc-kamchatka-2025-v1 is authentic, HTTP 200, digest-matched, and reports event 20250729_0000311/source_id 1838723 with magnitude 8.8, origin time 2025-07-29T23:24:51.44Z, latitude 52.6050, longitude 160.0725, and depth 20 km.\", \"The two authority records are from distinct hosts and required classes, and they materially agree on the same Kamchatka event: same date/region, same magnitude 8.8, origin times ~1 second apart, and epicenters separated by a small distance relative to earthquake catalog tolerances.\", \"No authenticated observation materially contradicts the claim; depth differs between catalogs, but the covenant requires comparison and material conflict screening, and the event identity, time, magnitude, and location remain materially compatible for the bounded remedy.\"], \"provenance_commitment\": \"86ba15a5a6e2a85822d121fcec108c5e5f22f8de218d14445f0adeadeefc0846\", \"snapshot_states\": [{\"finding\": \"USGS authenticated QuakeML reports earthquake us6000qw60 at Mww 8.8, origin time 2025-07-29T23:24:52.483Z, 52.4948 latitude, 160.2395 longitude, depth 35 km, off Kamchatka.\", \"snapshot_key\": \"usgs-kamchatka-2025-v1\", \"state\": \"SUPPORTS_BREACH\"}, {\"finding\": \"EMSC authenticated JSON reports event 20250729_0000311/source_id 1838723 at Mw 8.8, origin time 2025-07-29T23:24:51.44Z, 52.6050 latitude, 160.0725 longitude, depth 20 km, OFF EAST COAST OF KAMCHATKA.\", \"snapshot_key\": \"emsc-kamchatka-2025-v1\", \"state\": \"SUPPORTS_BREACH\"}], \"summary\": \"Authenticated USGS and EMSC records from distinct required authorities both identify the same 2025-07-29 Kamchatka earthquake with magnitude 8.8, origin times about 1.04 seconds apart, and nearby epicenters. The records materially agree on event identity, time, and location, satisfying the covenant threshold of magnitude 8.0 or greater. The requested read-only action at intensity 60 for 20 minutes is within the bounded remedy limits of intensity no greater than 80 for no more than two hours on the demonstration adapter.\"}"
    },
    "verdict": {
      "adjudicated_at": 1791834177,
      "applied_covenant_clauses": [
        "Evidence policy satisfied via authenticated, digest-matched authority snapshots from distinct registered USGS and EMSC hosts with required authority classes.",
        "Remedy policy satisfied because independently operated USGS and EMSC catalogs both identify the same seismic event at magnitude 8.0 or greater with materially compatible origin time and location.",
        "Requested consequence is proportionate because ENTER_READ_ONLY seeks intensity 60, below the cap of 80, and the claim specifies a 20-minute duration, below the two-hour maximum."
      ],
      "case_digest": "7c8b781d794c3696b92c92c10e3db33303570d4e9bea43b24e20f4c83b4caa9d",
      "covenant_digest": "7d6317c7325b38290a21fcb053d09c9ba31783168a672c7774a6d44622db3b8a",
      "decision": "BREACH_PROVEN",
      "findings": [
        "USGS snapshot usgs-kamchatka-2025-v1 is authentic, HTTP 200, digest-matched, and reports event us6000qw60 with magnitude 8.8, origin time 2025-07-29T23:24:52.483Z, latitude 52.4948, longitude 160.2395, and depth 35 km.",
        "EMSC snapshot emsc-kamchatka-2025-v1 is authentic, HTTP 200, digest-matched, and reports event 20250729_0000311/source_id 1838723 with magnitude 8.8, origin time 2025-07-29T23:24:51.44Z, latitude 52.6050, longitude 160.0725, and depth 20 km.",
        "The two authority records are from distinct hosts and required classes, and they materially agree on the same Kamchatka event: same date/region, same magnitude 8.8, origin times ~1 second apart, and epicenters separated by a small distance relative to earthquake catalog tolerances.",
        "No authenticated observation materially contradicts the claim; depth differs between catalogs, but the covenant requires comparison and material conflict screening, and the event identity, time, magnitude, and location remain materially compatible for the bounded remedy."
      ],
      "provenance_commitment": "86ba15a5a6e2a85822d121fcec108c5e5f22f8de218d14445f0adeadeefc0846",
      "snapshot_states": [
