          "snapshot_key": "usgs-kamchatka-2025-v1",
          "state": "SUPPORTS_BREACH"
        },
        {
          "finding": "EMSC authenticated JSON reports event 20250729_0000311/source_id 1838723 at Mw 8.8, origin time 2025-07-29T23:24:51.44Z, 52.6050 latitude, 160.0725 longitude, depth 20 km, OFF EAST COAST OF KAMCHATKA.",
          "snapshot_key": "emsc-kamchatka-2025-v1",
          "state": "SUPPORTS_BREACH"
        }
      ],
      "summary": "Authenticated USGS and EMSC records from distinct required authorities both identify the same 2025-07-29 Kamchatka earthquake with magnitude 8.8, origin times about 1.04 seconds apart, and nearby epicenters. The records materially agree on event identity, time, and location, satisfying the covenant threshold of magnitude 8.0 or greater. The requested read-only action at intensity 60 for 20 minutes is within the bounded remedy limits of intensity no greater than 80 for no more than two hours on the demonstration adapter."
    },
